" (https://assets.nationbuilder.com/plaid2016/pages/13170/attachments/original/1721133624/Plaid_Cymru_Maniffesto_2024_ENGLISH.pdf?1721133624=)\nciteturn23view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 72; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn22view1\",\"id\":18}); Total lines: 4392\nL0@P0: partyof.wales 1\nL1@P0: FOR FAIRNESS,\nL2@P0: FOR AMBITION,\nL3@P0: FOR WALES\nL4@P0: partyof.wales\nL5@P0: Plaid Cymru Manifesto for the\nL6@P0-1: Westminster General Election 20242 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL7@P1: Introduction\nL8@P1: Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL9@P1: By Rhun ap Iorwerth MS\nL10@P1: Plaid Cymru MPs have\nL11@P1: always been Wales’s\nL12@P1: voice in Westminster, not\nL13@P1: Westminster’s voice in\nL14@P1: Wales.\nL15@P1: This is not as good as it\nL16@P1: gets for our nation. The\nL17@P1: following pages set out our\nL18@P1: party’s vision of a fairer,\nL19@P1: more ambitious future where\nL20@P1: everyone can achieve their\nL21@P1: potential, regardless of\nL22@P1: circumstance or background.\nL23@P1: Being tied to Westminster\nL24@P1: means all risk and no reward\nL25@P1: for our nation. Wales is\nL26@P1: languishing at the bottom of\nL27@P1: too many league tables, our\nL28@P1: economy is stagnating, our\nL29@P1: transport network is creaking,\nL30@P1: and the lack of control over\nL31@P1: our natural resources means\nL32@P1: that we are energy-rich but\nL33@P1: fuel-poor.\nL34@P1: What sets Plaid Cymru apart\nL35@P1: is a record of not taking\nL36@P1: Wales for granted and always\nL37@P1: putting the interests of our\nL38@P1: communities and nation first.\nL39@P1: After 14 years of Tory cuts and\nL40@P1: weak opposition from Labour,\nL41@P1: Plaid Cymru offers a real\nL42@P1: alternative for Wales.\nL43@P1: We will fight every day for\nL44@P1: the billions owed to Wales\nL45@P1: from the HS2 high-speed rail\nL46@P1: project, and for a fair funding\nL47@P1: model which funds our\nL48@P1: country according to need, not\nL49@P1: population.\nL50@P1: This will enable us to invest\nL51@P1: in our public services and\nL52@P1: better reward our workforce.\nL53@P1: By supporting families\nL54@P1: and by devolving powers\nL55@P1: to ensure that more of the\nL56@P1: decisions that affect Wales\nL57@P1: are made in Wales, we will\nL58@P1: address the cost of living\nL59@P1: crisis and provide Welsh\nL60@P1: solutions to Welsh problems.\nL61@P1: Our ambition can be seen in\nL62@P1: our confidence that Wales\nL63@P1: can and should run its own\nL64@P1: affairs as an outward looking\nL65@P1: independent nation.\nL66@P1: Plaid Cymru is a party for\nL67@P1: the whole of Wales. Our\nL68@P1: candidates are rooted in\nL69@P1: their communities and\nL70@P1: passionate about overcoming\nL71@P1: the challenges facing our\nL72@P1: economy and public services.\nL73@P1: Wherever you live, you can\nL74@P1: be sure that a vote for Plaid\nL75@P1: Cymru on 4th July is a vote for\nL76@P1: a Member of Parliament who\nL77@P1: will always stand up for Wales’s\nL78@P1-2: best interests every day.partyof.wales 3\nL79@P2: Secure the £4bn owed to Wales from\nL80@P2: HS2 to invest in improving our own public\nL81@P2: transport in all parts of the country and\nL82@P2: reversing cuts to local bus services.\nL83@P2: Demand a fair funding system for Wales,\nL84@P2: based around our needs, giving us the\nL85@P2: public services we deserve.\nL86@P2: Fair funding from Westminster, enabling\nL87@P2: us to invest in our NHS workforce and\nL88@P2: recruit 500 GPs into Wales after years\nL89@P2: of Tory cuts and Labour mismanagement\nL90@P2: in Cardiff.\nL91@P2: A new Cancer Strategy to ensure cancers\nL92@P2: are caught and treated earlier, and ending\nL93@P2: Wales’s postcode lottery for treatment.\nL94@P2: Help 330,000 Welsh families to deal with\nL95@P2: the cost of living crisis by increasing\nL96@P2: Child Benefit by £20 per week. This will\nL97@P2: take 60,000 children out of poverty in\nL98@P2: Wales.\nL99@P2: Redressing economic unfairness;\nL100@P2: increasing windfall taxes and devolving\nL101@P2: the Crown Estate in order to create green\nL102@P2: jobs and build prosperity.\nL103@P2: FAIR\nL104@P2: FUNDING\nL105@P2: FOR WALES\nL106@P2: FAIR\nL107@P2: PLAY FOR\nL108@P2: PATIENTS\nL109@P2: FAIRNESS FOR\nL110@P2: FAMILIES AND\nL111@P2: COMMUNITIES\nL112@P2: “Plaid Cymru is a\nL113@P2: party for the whole of\nL114@P2: Wales. Our candidates\nL115@P2: are rooted in their\nL116@P2: communities and\nL117@P2: passionate about\nL118@P2: overcoming the\nL119@P2: challenges facing our\nL120@P2: economy and public\nL121@P2-3: services.”4 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL122@P3: Contents\nL123@P3: 6 Economy and Taxation\nL124@P3: 12 Health and Social Care\nL125@P3: 18 Education and Early Years\nL126@P3: 24 Criminal Justice and Policing\nL127@P3: 30 Housing and Planning\nL128@P3: 34 Climate Change and Energy\nL129@P3: 38 Welfare\nL130@P3: 42 Constitution and Governance\nL131@P3: 46 Rural Affairs\nL132@P3: 50 Foreign Affairs and Defence\nL133@P3: 54 Migration and Asylum\nL134@P3: 58 Transport\nL135@P3: 62 Culture, Media and Sport\nL136@P3: 66 Welsh Language\nL137@P3-4: 68 Equalitiespartyof.wales 5\nL138@P4: “Wherever you live, you\nL139@P4: can be sure that a vote\nL140@P4: for Plaid Cymru on\nL141@P4: 4th July is a vote for a\nL142@P4: Member of Parliament\nL143@P4: who will always stand\nL144@P4: up for Wales’s best\nL145@P4-5: interests every day.”6 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL146@P5: The past fourteen years of\nL147@P5: Conservative UK Government\nL148@P5: have been economically very\nL149@P5: damaging for people, families\nL150@P5: and business in Wales.\nL151@P5: 6 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL152@P5-6: Economy & Taxationpartyof.wales 7\nL153@P6: Under David Cameron, the\nL154@P6: Tory government pursued\nL155@P6: a financial programme\nL156@P6: of devastating cuts to\nL157@P6: public services in the\nL158@P6: name of austerity. The\nL159@P6: UK’s international trade\nL160@P6: was undermined by the\nL161@P6: hard Brexit pursued by\nL162@P6: both Theresa May and\nL163@P6: Boris Johnson. And then\nL164@P6: the economy was crashed\nL165@P6: completely by Liz Truss.\nL166@P6: We are living with the legacies\nL167@P6: of all of these examples of the\nL168@P6: Conservatives’ poor economic\nL169@P6: judgement, which are being\nL170@P6: echoed by a Labour Party that\nL171@P6: has already tied itself to their\nL172@P6: spending plans.\nL173@P6: So long as Wales remains a\nL174@P6: part of the UK, Plaid Cymru\nL175@P6: believes that the role of\nL176@P6: UK Government in Wales\nL177@P6: should be to provide enough\nL178@P6: financial support for our\nL179@P6: public services and to create\nL180@P6: the conditions for the kind of\nL181@P6: sustainable economic growth\nL182@P6: from which all people and\nL183@P6: communities can benefit,\nL184@P6: rather than just those at the\nL185@P6: top of the tree.\nL186@P6: This is not what UK\nL187@P6: Governments have\nL188@P6: delivered. Our public\nL189@P6: services are underfunded\nL190@P6: and have been hollowed\nL191@P6: out, and our economy has\nL192@P6: stagnated. These economic\nL193@P6: conditions have led to wholly\nL194@P6: unacceptable rising levels\nL195@P6: of child deprivation, with a\nL196@P6: heartbreaking one in three\nL197@P6: children now growing up in\nL198@P6: poverty.\nL199@P6-7: partyof.wales 78 Plaid Cymru Manifesto 2024\nL200@P7: A Fair Funding Formula\nL201@P7: Plaid Cymru believes\nL202@P7: that Wales should be\nL203@P7: funded according to our\nL204@P7: needs, not the out-dated\nL205@P7: Barnett Formula which\nL206@P7: instead provides funding\nL207@P7: proportionate to spending on\nL208@P7: England’s needs. We want\nL209@P7: to see a new needs-based\nL210@P7: funding formula introduced\nL211@P7: in place of the Barnett\nL212@P7: Formula.\nL213@P7: A Fairer Tax System\nL214@P7: We believe that Wales should\nL215@P7: have full control of economic\nL216@P7: levers, in order to grow and\nL217@P7: green our economy in a way\nL218@P7: that will have the greatest\nL219@P7: positive impact upon our\nL220@P7: communities. We want the\nL221@P7: Senedd to have powers to\nL222@P7: set income tax bands and\nL223@P7: thresholds, as they already\nL224@P7: do in Scotland, so that we\nL225@P7: can create a system that fits\nL226@P7: Wales’s circumstances.\nL227@P7: At a UK level, we want\nL228@P7: to see the balance of the\nL229@P7: tax burden fall on those\nL230@P7: individuals and corporations\nL231@P7: with the broadest shoulders\nL232@P7: bearing a fairer share of\nL233@P7: overall tax paid, rather than\nL234@P7: those with less means.\nL235@P7: In recent years, we have\nL236@P7: seen some industries\nL237@P7: substantially increase their\nL238@P7: profits because of market\nL239@P7: conditions and not as a result\nL240@P7: of their own investment\nL241@P7: and endeavours. These\nL242@P7: sectors, which have included\nL243@P7: oil and gas producers and\nL244@P7: energy companies, should\nL245@P7: be appropriately taxed,\nL246@P7: particularly where there is\nL247@P7: an effective monopoly or\nL248@P7: cartel which controls the\nL249@P7: product. In particular, we\nL250@P7: think that energy companies\nL251@P7: should be subject to an\nL252@P7: increased windfall tax, and\nL253@P7: will close loopholes which\nL254@P7: they currently exploit to\nL255@P7: avoid this. At the same time,\nL256@P7: we will promote renewable\nL257@P7: energy investment as an\nL258@P7: alternative.\nL259@P7: We would re-introduce the\nL260@P7: cap on bankers’ bonuses.\nL261@P7: Plaid Cymru would equalise\nL262@P7: capital gains tax with\nL263@P7: income tax, raising between\nL264@P7: £12bn - £15bn. We would\nL265@P7: investigate increasing higher\nL266@P7: earners’ National Insurance\nL267@P7: contributions, and support\nL268@P7: introducing a wealth tax.\nL269@P7: We would crack down on\nL270@P7: tax evasion and avoidance,\nL271@P7: and abolish loopholes for\nL272@P7: non-doms.\nL273@P7: Ambitions for our Economy\nL274@P7: In the run up to the 2026\nL275@P7: Senedd elections, we will set\nL276@P7: new targets for the Welsh\nL277@P7: economy so that we can\nL278@P7: better understand the impact\nL279@P7: of policy decisions and\nL280@P7: investment choices through\nL281@P7: their outcomes, rather than\nL282@P7: ticking boxes on process.\nL283@P7: Recognising the inequality\nL284@P7: in economic performance\nL285@P7: of different nations and\nL286@P7: regions in the UK, Plaid\nL287@P7: Cymru propose an Economic\nL288@P7: Fairness Bill that will make\nL289@P7: levelling up a meaningful\nL290@P7: phrase, rather than a political\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://s3-eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/www.snp.org/uploads/2024/06/2024-06-20b-SNP-General-Election-Manifesto-2024_interactive.pdf)\nciteturn23view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 32; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn22view0\",\"id\":23}); Total lines: 1228\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://assets.nationbuilder.com/reformuk/pages/253/attachments/original/1718625371/Reform_UK_Our_Contract_with_You.pdf)\nciteturn23view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 28; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn22view0\",\"id\":24}); Total lines: 1182\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Wealth of Our Nation: Restore Britain’s Economic Philosophy.docx (https://assets.nationbuilder.com/restorebritain/pages/1255/attachments/original/1785930638/The_Wealth_of_Our_Nation__Restore_Britain%E2%80%99s_Economic_Philosophy.pdf?1785930638=)\nciteturn23view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 64; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn22view2\",\"id\":4}); Total lines: 1252\n---------------------------------------------